{"packSlug":"ca-federal","packName":"Canada (federal)","jurisdiction":"CA","ruleKey":"ca-email-unsubscribe","kind":"required_notice","severity":"require","appliesTo":["email"],"title":"Canada: working unsubscribe link in every marketing email [COUNSEL][VERIFY]","ownerExplanation":"Marketing emails to Canadian recipients must include a working unsubscribe mechanism, and the request must be honoured promptly. Vireek checks that the unsubscribe wording is present; the legal honouring deadline is for counsel to define. [COUNSEL][VERIFY]","params":{"noticeId":"ca-unsubscribe-mechanism","text":"Add a one-step unsubscribe link or address that works for at least 60 days after sending, and honour requests promptly. [COUNSEL][VERIFY]"},"sourceRefs":[{"citation":"Canada's Anti-Spam Legislation (CASL), S.C. 2010, c. 23","type":"statute","note":"Starter citation — [COUNSEL][VERIFY] confirm current text, scope and effective dates before approving."},{"citation":"Electronic Commerce Protection Regulations (CRTC) and Industry Canada regulations under CASL","type":"regulation","note":"Starter citation — [COUNSEL][VERIFY] confirm current text, scope and effective dates before approving."}]},
